\maketitle

\section{Introduction}
The code suh (Glottocode suba1254, listed as ``Suba (Retired)'') could not be tied to a living language. ISO 639-3 change request 2007-031 created suh together with ssc (Suba-Simbiti) and sxb (Suba) in 2008. The searches did not show what status suh has now, and they found no Glottolog record for suba1254. The ``Bookkeeping'' family label is a Glottolog placeholder, and the sources give no reason to link it to a particular language. The only well-documented Suba is the Bantu language of Kenya (sxb), covered in the resources below. It is not confirmed to be what suh refers to.

\section{Primary Educational Resources}
None found for suh. For Kenyan Suba (sxb), the Wikipedia article reports that the Kenyan government introduced Suba as a primary school subject in the 1990s. The search turned up no textbooks.

\section{Linguistic and Reference Materials}
\begin{itemize}
\item ISO 639-3 Registration Authority, 2007 change request: \url{https://glottolog.org/resource/reference/id/iso6393:2007-031}
\item Wikipedia, Suba language (sxb): \url{https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Suba_language}
\item Omniglot, Suba (Olusuba): \url{https://omniglot.com/writing/suba.htm}
\end{itemize}

\section{Religious and Community Resources}
The Wikipedia article on the Kenyan Suba people says a Suba New Testament was published in 2010: \url{https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Suba_people_(Kenya)}

\section{Digital and Audio Resources}
Kenyan Suba (sxb) revitalisation coverage: a Nation Africa report, \url{https://www.nation.africa/kenya/counties/homa-bay/-push-to-save-dying-suba-language-now-gathers-momentum-4128100}, and an IJNet story on a radio station working to keep the language alive, \url{https://ijnet.org/en/story/radio-station-kenya-works-keep-endangered-language-alive}.

\section{Curriculum Development Context}
For suh itself, nothing could be established. If the target is the Kenyan Suba language, the resources above are a starting point, but no dictionary or grammar was found in this search.
\end{document}
